WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.109
David, who is responsible for the destruction
of the Republican Party?

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:09.040
The first question is, has the Republican
Party been destroyed?

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.450
It's not clear.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.090
Most Trump, most Republican voters still support
Trump.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.110
So it remains to be seen.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:21.550
However, yes, Trump lost the White House in
twenty eighteen.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.920
Trump's nonsense lost the House for Republicans
in 2020.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.580
Trump's nonsense lost the Senate for Republicans.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.199
So that's true.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:36.700
But I don't think the vast majority of the
blame should go to Trump.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.210
It's the voters who put Trump in who were
radicalized by the right wing media whose

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.559
influence grows and grows and grows.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:51.940
And it was abetted by the Republican officials
who stood by and mostly let let Trump do his

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.940
thing.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.649
So, yes, Trump's actions were bad and Trump's
actions are responsible for him losing in

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:00.160
2020.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.520
And Trump lost them the house in twenty eighteen
in the Senate in 2020.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:10.560
But the real responsibility lies with those
who allowed Trump to get in in the first place

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:16.680
due to voters who voted for him and Republican
elected officials who stood aside and right

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.700
wing media that cheerlead the entire thing.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.830
And in a way, you can sort of say that this
started with the radicalization under Ronald

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.159
Reagan in the early 1980s.

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:33.759
It was accelerated by Newt Gingrich in the
mid 90s, who Newt Gingrich really brought

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.700
in this style of politics that was owned.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:37.700
The Libs.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.700
I mean, now that's what it's called.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.770
They didn't call it that in the mid 90s, but
Newt Gingrich's idea was just obstruct Democrats

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:51.400
for the sake of obstruction, opposed Democrats
on everything for the sake of opposition.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:59.670
And that's how we went from Nixon, who created
the EPA to Jim Inhofe in the Senate holding

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:05.950
a snowball, claiming it to be evidence that
global warming and climate change aren't something

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.460
we need to worry about.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.590
So there are feedback loops here, and it can
be hard to say exactly where it started and

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.090
what's responsible.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:17.870
Trump is hugely guilty for damaging the Republican
Party, but Trump doesn't get to be president

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:23.349
or even Republican nominee where he not enabled
by Republican voters and right wing media.

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:29.250
And those are the very same Republicans who
now are partially radicalized because Donald

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.540
Trump's way of thinking about politics was
a signal boosted by right wing media over

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.140
the last four years.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.410
So when I really think about blame in terms
of the future of the Republican Party, which

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:46.280
is still a question mark, Trump was and has
been exactly who we believed that he was.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.989
Now, a lot of right wing voters didn't believe
it, but we knew who Trump was.

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:53.319
He doesn't care about anybody but himself.

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:59.459
He ignored what is his real job and instead
lobbed attacks at enemies, didn't do the things

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:02.850
he had to do, mishandled every major challenge.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.740
And then when he lost eventually, which was
the right outcome based on his actions, he

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.849
blamed everybody else for that as well.

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:15.390
And when we say who who is ultimately really
responsible, it is Trump, but it's right wing

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:21.260
media and it's Republican elected officials
who could have stopped this a long time ago.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.700
And it's Republican voters as well.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.560
And that leads us to what is a rebuilt Republican
Party look like.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.230
I don't know how the Republican Party comes
together to rebuild to the extent that they're

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.650
now out of power in the House, Senate and
White House.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:44.470
How do they rebuild without dealing with the
Q and on a Newsmax Trumpy wing?

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.150
I don't know the answer to that, but we have
time to look at that.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.530
It is the beginning of the Biden era.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:56.200
Come Monday, I will have a report for you
about has Joe Biden gotten done the things

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.920
he said were week one and day one priorities.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.230
This is a different phase, but we will see
what the future of the Republican Party is.

